Z||000005||BN Boomer||10-09-2001||03:31 PM||||Not a bad little truck. Toyotas are decent, reliable cars and trucks, but I'd rather have a domestic brand, too (Even though my new Impala was made in Ontario, Canada). I've looked at and would probably go with a Ford SuperDuty Powerstroke if I were going to buy a new truck to replace my Suburban.<P>I think my next "truck" is going to be another 2 seater project vehicle, but one far less common than a Fiero: a Jeep CJ-8 Scrambler. There were only just over 26,000 made during the entire five years they were in production from 81-86. They have almost become collector vehicles and are difficult to find in good condition at a reasonable price.||||reg||1
